    ~A Text File (.txt) and a compressed image folder
    ~A Spreadsheet math formula and an output PDF
}

// Chapter: Digital Documentation | Difficulty: medium
::Cell Reference vs Cell Range::
In electronic spreadsheets, how does a Cell Reference differ from a Cell Range?
[difficulty:medium]
[chapter:Digital Documentation]
[tags:spreadsheet,references]
{
    =A Cell Reference is the unique address of a single cell (e.g., A1), while a Cell Range is a collection of contiguous cells separated by a colon (e.g., A1:C5)
    ~A Cell Reference represents rows, while a Cell Range represents columns
    ~A Cell Reference is letters only, while a Cell Range is numbers only
    ~A Cell Reference is for formulas, while a Cell Range is for functions
}

