::L2 GIMP Layer Offsets 5::
In GIMP, when creating a 3D depth effect on text using duplicate layers, if you offset the lower layer horizontally by \(5\) pixels, how does it affect the illusion of thickness?
[difficulty:hard]
[chapter:Graphics in ICT]
[tags:gimp,3d_effect,coordinates]
{
    =It increases the perceived depth or thickness by \(5\) units along the X-axis
    ~It changes the overall image resolution from RGB to grayscale
    ~It automatically crops the canvas to fit the main text boundary
    ~It deletes the alpha channel from the active layer mask
}

